+## More accepting swipes and softer failed returns (2026-10-04)
+
+Requirements **R01/V03/V04/V05/Q01**. The owner requests greater acceptance sensitivity and a smoother transition when the page returns to its original position. Commitment now requires **20 logical units**, down from 32 (37.5% less travel). A committed stroke survives relaxation until an actual MOVE returns within **six units** instead of twelve. Horizontal intent requires only a 1.05 ratio of horizontal to vertical travel rather than 1.15; mostly vertical gestures still do not claim the page. Six-unit initial claim and release-accounting safeguards remain.
+
+Failed interior page swipes now animate over **0.42-0.52 seconds**, replacing the 0.28-0.38-second sine return. One smootherstep progress value moves both current and neighboring content and closes the gutter; its velocity and acceleration are zero at both ends. It preserves the held positions exactly on release and does not overshoot. The fixed header, full adjacent page preview, 64-unit growing gutter, successful-arrival easing and outer-edge carousel-style spring retain their existing behavior. No physics, replay, backend, account or ad behavior change.
